5.6 |\n| H4C12 | ENSG00000273542 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 2 | 0.1 | 7043887585.6 |\n| H4C6 | ENSG00000274618 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 2 | 0.4 | 7043887585.6 |\n| H4C9 | ENSG00000276180 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 2 | 0.1 | 7043887585.6 |\n| H4C5 | ENSG00000276966 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 2 | 1.4 | 7043887585.6 |\n| H4C4 | ENSG00000277157 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 2 | 0.6 | 7043887585.6 |\n| H4C1 | ENSG00000278637 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 2 | 1.8 | 7043887585.6 |\n| H4C2 | ENSG00000278705 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 2 | 0.2 | 7043887585.6 |\n| LTF | ENSG00000012223 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 15 | 1132.8 | 6268778890.5 |\n| MPO | ENSG00000005381 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 16 | 5.0 | 3178365350.9 |\n| HBA2 | ENSG00000188536 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 17 | 15.3 | 2646963892.0 |\n| HBA1 | ENSG00000206172 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 17 | 7.6 | 2646963892.0 |\n| MYH9 | ENSG00000100345 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 19 | 1873.8 | 2287762683.6 |\n| MYH14 | ENSG00000105357 | Top 20 genes by DVP Intensity \u2014 neutrophils | 20 | 6.6 | 2266032455.1 |\n\nFigure 1 (a44): scatter (RNA nCPM (cardiomyocytes) (log) vs DVP Intensity (cardiomyocytes) (log)) from a40\nFigure 2 (a45): scatter (RNA nCPM (hepatocytes) (log) vs DVP Intensity (hepatocytes) (log)) from a41\nFigure 3 (a46): scatter (RNA nCPM (neutrophils) (log) vs DVP Intensity (neutrophils) (log)) from a42\nFigure 4 (a62): bar (Cell type vs Top-20 overlap count) from a59\nFigure 5 (a66): heatmap from a65\n\n**Findings**\n\n- RNA\u2013protein rank agreement is weak across all three cell types. Spearman r = 0.097 (cardiomyocytes, n=4714, p=2.25\u00d710\u207b\u00b9\u00b9), 0.354 (hepatocytes, n=5985, p=3.23\u00d710\u207b\u00b9\u2077\u2076), and 0.153 (neutrophils, n=5396, p=1.79\u00d710\u207b\u00b2\u2079). All correlations are statistically significant but indicate poor rank concordance between single-cell-type RNA nCPM and DVP cell-type Intensity. (evidence: a83 row 0: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, count=4714, r=0.0972, p_value=2.25e-11; row 1: cell_type=hepatocytes, count=5985, r=0.354, p_value=3.23e-176; row 2: cell_type=neutrophils, count=5396, r=0.1526, p_value=1.79e-29)\n- Top-20 overlap is minimal: 3 of 20 genes shared (Jaccard = 0.081) for cardiomyocytes, 1 of 20 (Jaccard = 0.026) for hepatocytes, and 0 of 20 (Jaccard = 0) for neutrophils. The cardiomyocyte overlap genes are TTN, MYH7, and MYBPC3; the hepatocyte overlap gene is ALB. (evidence: a83 row 0: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, overlap=3, jaccard=0.0810811; row 1: cell_type=hepatocytes, overlap=1, jaccard=0.025641; row 2: cell_type=neutrophils, overlap=0, jaccard=0)\n- The most discordant genes are dominated by histone variants (H4C15, H4C6, H4C1, H4C8, H4C14) and secreted/cytosolic proteins (ALB, EEF1A2, PDZRN3, TXNIP, SDHA). These genes show |RNA percentile \u2212 protein percentile| > 0.97, meaning they rank near the extreme of one modality but near the bottom of the other. For example, ALB in cardiomyocytes has RNA percentile 0.0002 (rank 1 of 4714) but protein percentile 0.997 (rank 4701), reflecting its role as a secreted protein with high DVP signal but negligible cardiomyocyte-specific RNA. (evidence: a81 row 0: gene=ALB, cell_type=cardiomyocytes, signed_diff=-0.99703, abs_diff=0.99703, rna_pct=0.000212134, prot_pct=0.997242, Main location=Endoplasmic reticulum;Golgi apparatus, rank_2=4701; row 1: gene=ACTBL2, cell_type=cardiomyocytes, signed_diff=-0.986848, abs_diff=0.986848, rna_pct=0.000212134, prot_pct=0.98706, Main location=\u2014, rank_2=4653; row 2: gene=H4C15, cell_type=cardiomyocytes, signed_diff=-0.977514, abs_diff=0.977514, rna_pct=0.000212134, prot_pct=0.977726, Main location=\u2014, rank_2=4609; row 3: gene=H4C6, cell_type=cardiomyocytes, signed_diff=-0.977514, abs_diff=0.977514, rna_pct=0.000212134, prot_pct=0.977726, Main location=\u2014, rank_2=4609; row 4: gene=PDZRN3, cell_type=cardiomyocytes, signed_diff=0.97221, abs_diff=0.97221, rna_pct=0.990454, prot_pct=0.0182435, Main location=Cytosol, rank_2=86; row 5: gene=EEF1A2, cell_type=hepatocytes, signed_diff=-0.995823, abs_diff=0.995823, rna_pct=0.000167084, prot_pct=0.99599, Main location=Cytosol, rank_2=5961; row 6: gene=H4C1, cell_type=hepatocytes, signed_diff=-0.991646, abs_diff=0.991646, rna_pct=0.000167084, prot_pct=0.991813, Main location=\u2014, rank_2=5936; row 7: gene=H4C8, cell_type=hepatocytes, signed_diff=-0.976441, abs_diff=0.976441, rna_pct=0.0153718, prot_pct=0.991813, Main location=\u2014, rank_2=5936; row 8: gene=H4C14, cell_type=hepatocytes, signed_diff=-0.976441, abs_diff=0.976441, rna_pct=0.0153718, prot_pct=0.991813, Main location=\u2014, rank_2=5936; row 9: gene=SDHA, cell_type=hepatocytes, signed_diff=-0.971094, abs_diff=0.971094, rna_pct=0.000167084, prot_pct=0.971261, Main location=Mitochondria, rank_2=5813; row 10: gene=H4C15, cell_type=neutrophils, signed_diff=-0.997405, abs_diff=0.997405, rna_pct=0.000185322, prot_pct=0.997591, Main location=\u2014, rank_2=5383; row 11: gene=H4C12, cell_type=neutrophils, signed_diff=-0.997405, abs_diff=0.997405, rna_pct=0.000185322, prot_pct=0.997591, Main location=\u2014, rank_2=5383; \u2026 3 more rows)\n- Hepatocytes show the strongest (though still modest) RNA\u2013protein agreement (r = 0.354), consistent with the liver's high abundance of secreted proteins (ALB, FGA, FGB, TTR, AMBP) that are well captured by both modalities. Neutrophils show the weakest top-20 overlap (zero shared genes), with the RNA top-20 dominated by mitochondrial genes (MT-CO3, MT-CO2, MT-CYB, MT-ATP6, MT-ND2, MT-ND1) and the protein top-20 dominated by histone variants (H4C5, H4C4, H4C1, H4C2) and structural proteins (MYH9, MYH14). (evidence: a83 row 1: cell_type=hepatocytes, r=0.354, overlap=1; row 2: cell_type=neutrophils, r=0.1526, overlap=0)\n\n**Limitations**\n\n- Spearman correlation measures rank concordance across all retained genes; it does not capture whether absolute expression levels agree or whether the relationship is linear on any scale.\n- DVP cell-type Intensity is a deconvolved estimate from tissue-level imaging, not a direct single-cell measurement; its resolution and dynamic range differ fundamentally from scRNA-seq nCPM.\n- The top-20 overlap and Jaccard metrics are sensitive to the arbitrary cutoff of 20; a different list size would yield different overlap values.\n- Histone variant genes (H4C1\u2013H4C15) appear as separate Ensembl entries with near-identical RNA nCPM values (all tied at the same rank), which inflates their representation in the discordant-gene list; they may represent a single biological signal split across paralog entries.\n- Subcellular location annotations are available for only 6 of the 14 unique discordant genes; the remaining 8 have no annotation in the HPA subcellular location table.\n- The analysis uses the HPA master table as the gene universe; genes absent from this table (e.g., some pseudogenes or recently annotated loci) are excluded.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- a1 data \"RNA nCPM \u2014 cardiomyocytes, hepatocytes, neutrophils\" (20162 rows) from investigator_hpa\n- a2 data \"DVP Intensity \u2014 cardiomyocytes, hepatocytes, neutrophils\" (19297 rows) from investigator_hpa\n- a3 data \"RNA nCPM + DVP Intensity joined on Ensembl ID\" (19297 rows) from join of a1, a2\n- a4 data \"Retained genes \u2014 cardiomyocytes (RNA nCPM > 0 AND DVP Intensity > 0)\" (4714 rows) from filter of a3\n- a5 data \"Retained genes \u2014 hepatocytes (RNA nCPM > 0 AND DVP Intensity > 0)\" (5985 rows) from filter of a3\n- a6 data \"Retained genes \u2014 neutrophils (RNA nCPM > 0 AND DVP Intensity > 0)\" (5396 rows) from filter of a3\n- a7 data \"Top 20 genes by RNA nCPM \u2014 cardiomyocytes\" (20 rows) from 